    <h1>🌟 The Ultimate Interview Cheat Sheet 🌟</h1>
    <p>Prepare for your next job interview with these essential tips and tricks!</p>

    <hr>

    <h2>Part 1: Pre-Interview Preparation</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><b>Research the Company:</b> Understand their mission, products, and recent news.</li>
        <li><b>Know Your Resume:</b> Be ready to talk about every point on your resume.</li>
        <li><b>Practice Your Answers:</b> Prepare for common questions like "Tell me about yourself" and "Why do you want to work here?".</li>
    </ul>

    <hr>

    <h2>Part 2: During the Interview</h2>
    <ol>
        <li><b>Arrive on Time:</b> Be punctual, whether it's an in-person or virtual interview.</li>
        <li><b>Listen Carefully:</b> Pay attention to the questions and the interviewer's cues.</li>
        <li><b>Be Honest and Confident:</b> Answer questions truthfully and show enthusiasm.</li>
    </ol>

    <hr>

    <h2>Common Questions to Practice</h2>
    <h3>Behavioral Questions</h3>
    <p>These questions assess your past behavior to predict future performance. Use the <b>STAR</b> method (Situation, Task, Action, Result).</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Tell me about a time you faced a challenge.</li>
        <li>Describe a time you worked well in a team.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Technical Questions</h3>
    <p>Be ready for questions specific to your field. For example, a web developer might be asked about JavaScript frameworks or database design.</p>
    <p>For more in-depth technical guides, check out these <a href="https://example.com/tech-resources">technical interview resources</a>.</p>

